# Experimentation and pilot evaluation

**Business questions:** should we launch a lower free-delivery threshold, and should we scale a rider-batching pilot?

> **Simulated data.** Everything comes from a seeded Python generator (`data_gen/generate.py`, seed {{ cfg.sim.seed }}), not from any real company. Assumptions: {{ cfg.sim.users }} users with gamma-Poisson order rates, lognormal basket sizes and a propensity for small high-margin baskets; a {{ cfg.sim.pre_period_days }}-day pre-period under the current policy; users randomised 50/50 on first visit during a {{ cfg.sim.assignment_days }}-day assignment week and observed for {{ cfg.sim.observation_days }} days; delivery fee {{ cfg.promo.delivery_fee }} below the free threshold and a cost to serve of {{ cfg.promo.delivery_cost }} per order. The pilot is a daily panel of {{ cfg.sim.pilot_nodes }} nodes ({{ cfg.sim.pilot_treated }} randomly chosen for batching) over {{ cfg.sim.pilot_pre_days }} days before and {{ cfg.sim.pilot_post_days }} after the switch-on, with shared seasonality and shocks.

